# AlgoViz — Cursor Rules

## Project Identity
This is **AlgoViz**: a fully local, hostable algorithm visualizer.
It accepts source code in multiple languages, lets the user pin specific
variables via a gutter checkbox in the editor, traces execution, and renders
those variables' step-by-step mutations as animated visual panels.

Architecture: npm monorepo → packages/core | packages/tracer | packages/renderer | packages/app

---

## Non-Negotiables

- **Never skip tests.** Every exported function and component gets a test. If a
  phase task does not mention tests, write them anyway.
- **Never modify more than one package at a time** without stating which packages
  are affected and why at the start of your response.
- **Never use `any` in TypeScript.** Use `unknown` and narrow it, or define a type.
- **Never hardcode file paths.** Use path constants or environment variables.
- **Never leave a TODO without a GitHub-issue-style description:**
  `// TODO(#issue): <what> — <why blocked>`
- **Never use hardcoded hex colours in components.** Always use the CSS custom
  property tokens defined in `packages/app/src/styles/tokens.css`.

---

## Tech Stack Constraints

| Concern          | Tool                              | Notes                                      |
|------------------|-----------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| Monorepo         | npm workspaces                    | Root `package.json` manages all            |
| Frontend build   | Vite                              | Dev + optimised prod build                 |
| UI framework     | React 18 + TypeScript strict      | Functional components + hooks only         |
| Styling          | Tailwind CSS                      | Extend with Catppuccin Mocha tokens        |
| Colour theme     | Catppuccin Mocha                  | See token table below — no other palette   |
| Animation        | Framer Motion                     | Cell transitions and highlights            |
| Graph/tree viz   | D3.js                             | Only for non-array structures              |
| Code editor      | CodeMirror 6 (`@codemirror/view`) | Custom gutter extension for variable pins  |
| State            | Zustand                           | One store per package, no prop drilling    |
| Frontend tests   | Vitest + React Testing Library    | Co-located `*.test.tsx` files              |
| Backend          | FastAPI (Python 3.11+)            | Fully local — never binds to 0.0.0.0      |
| Python tracer    | `sys.settrace`                    | Primary language                           |
| JS tracer        | Node.js `vm` + Proxy observers    | Called via subprocess from FastAPI         |
| Java tracer      | Source instrumentation + `javac`  | Called via subprocess from FastAPI         |
| C# tracer        | Roslyn Scripting API              | Called via subprocess from FastAPI         |
| Backend tests    | pytest + pytest-asyncio           | Mirror src structure in `/tests`           |
| Parsing          | tree-sitter (WASM in browser)     | Language-agnostic, one grammar per lang    |
| Linting          | ESLint (airbnb-ts) + Prettier     | Run before every commit                    |
| Git commits      | Conventional Commits              | feat/fix/chore/test/docs/refactor          |
| Hosting          | Docker Compose                    | One container for app, one for tracer      |

---

## Catppuccin Mocha — Colour Tokens

All components must use these CSS custom properties. Define them in
`packages/app/src/styles/tokens.css` and extend Tailwind's config to expose
them as utility classes (e.g. `bg-ctp-base`, `text-ctp-text`).

```css
:root {
  --ctp-base:      #1e1e2e;
  --ctp-mantle:    #181825;
  --ctp-crust:     #11111b;
  --ctp-surface0:  #313244;
  --ctp-surface1:  #45475a;
  --ctp-surface2:  #585b70;
  --ctp-overlay0:  #6c7086;
  --ctp-overlay1:  #7f849c;
  --ctp-overlay2:  #9399b2;
  --ctp-subtext0:  #a6adc8;
  --ctp-subtext1:  #bac2de;
  --ctp-text:      #cdd6f4;
  --ctp-lavender:  #b4befe;
  --ctp-blue:      #89b4fa;
  --ctp-sapphire:  #74c7ec;
  --ctp-sky:       #89dceb;
  --ctp-teal:      #94e2d5;
  --ctp-green:     #a6e3a1;
  --ctp-yellow:    #f9e2af;
  --ctp-peach:     #fab387;
  --ctp-maroon:    #eba0ac;
  --ctp-red:       #f38ba8;
  --ctp-mauve:     #cba6f7;
  --ctp-pink:      #f5c2e7;
  --ctp-flamingo:  #f2cdcd;
  --ctp-rosewater: #f5e0dc;
}
```

Semantic mappings (enforce throughout):
- Page background         → `--ctp-base`
- Panel / card background → `--ctp-mantle` or `--ctp-surface0`
- Editor background       → `--ctp-crust`
- Border / divider        → `--ctp-surface1`
- Muted text / labels     → `--ctp-subtext0`
- Primary text            → `--ctp-text`
- Highlighted cell        → `--ctp-mauve` bg, `--ctp-base` text
- Active/selected accent  → `--ctp-lavender`
- Error state             → `--ctp-red`
- Running / success       → `--ctp-green`
- Pinned gutter marker    → `--ctp-blue`
- Playback controls bg    → `--ctp-surface1`
- Primary button          → `--ctp-mauve`
- Primary button hover    → `--ctp-lavender`

The CodeMirror editor theme must also use Catppuccin Mocha. Use
`@catppuccin/codemirror` if the package exists; otherwise define a custom
`EditorView.theme({})` object using the tokens above.

---

## Gutter Variable Selection — Design Contract

The code editor renders a custom CodeMirror 6 gutter to the left of line numbers.
This gutter shows an interactive marker on every line that contains a variable
declaration or assignment.

Behaviour rules:
- Markers appear **only on lines that declare or assign a variable**, detected via
  the tree-sitter AST after each keystroke (debounced 300 ms)
- Unselected marker: small hollow circle in `--ctp-overlay0`
- Selected (pinned) marker: filled circle in `--ctp-blue` with a subtle
  `--ctp-blue` left-border highlight on the line
- Clicking a marker toggles its pinned state
- Multiple variables may be pinned simultaneously
- Primitives (int, str, bool, float) are pinnable — displayed as a single-cell
  panel showing their current value as a string representation
- Pin state lives in a CodeMirror `StateField` — not React state
- On each editor change, re-run AST detection and refresh which lines have
  markers; preserve pins on lines that still have a valid declaration
- Pinned variable names are exposed to the parent React component via a stable
  callback ref so the parent can read them before submitting a trace request
- The API request body includes `trackedVariables: string[]` derived from the
  pinned set; the tracer filters its output to only those variables

