## File & Folder Conventions

```
packages/
  core/
    src/
      parsers/          # python.ts, javascript.ts, java.ts, csharp.ts
      detectors/        # structureDetector.ts, roleInferrer.ts
      differ/           # snapshotDiffer.ts
      types/            # index.ts — all shared TS interfaces
    tests/
  tracer/
    src/
      main.py
      tracer.py
      sandbox.py
      models.py
      languages/        # python_tracer.py, js_tracer.py, java_tracer.py, csharp_tracer.py
    tests/
  renderer/
    src/
      components/       # ArrayPanel, MatrixPanel, GraphPanel, PrimitivePanel …
      hooks/            # usePlayback.ts, useSnapshot.ts, useTrace.ts
      store/            # vizStore.ts
      utils/            # diffHighlighter.ts
    tests/
  app/
    src/
      pages/            # index.tsx
      components/       # CodeEditor (with gutter), LanguageSelector, ControlBar
      styles/           # tokens.css, globals.css
      examples/         # sample algorithms per language
    tests/
```

- Component files: `PascalCase.tsx`
- Hook files: `camelCase.ts` prefixed with `use`
- Utility files: `camelCase.ts`
- Test files: mirror source name + `.test.tsx` or `.test.ts`
- Python files: `snake_case.py`

---

## TypeScript Rules

- `strict: true` always
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions and aliases
- All cross-package interfaces live in `packages/core/src/types/index.ts`
- Named exports only from utility and type files
- Default exports allowed only for React components and the FastAPI app object

---

## React Rules

- Functional components only
- Props interface defined above the component in the same file
- No component exceeds 150 lines — split if larger
- Custom hooks must have tests mocking stores or API calls
- Never fetch inside a component — use a hook or store action
- CodeMirror instance created with `useRef` + `useEffect` — never re-created on re-render

---

## Testing Rules

- Minimum coverage: **80%** for all packages
- Unit: one function or component in isolation
- Integration: parser → detector → snapshot pipeline end-to-end
- All tests must pass before a phase is marked complete
- Use `describe` blocks grouped by feature
- Gutter extension logic tested via CodeMirror `EditorState` directly
  (pure state machine — no browser required)

---

## Git Discipline

- One commit per logical unit of work
- Format: `type(scope): short description`
- Never commit to `main` — feature branches only
- Branch naming: `phase-1/scaffold`, `phase-2/tracer`, etc.
- Phase merges only when all tests pass and coverage is met

---

## Agentic Behaviour Rules

- **Before writing code**, state the plan in 3–5 bullets
- **After completing a task**, list what was created/modified and what tests were added
- If a task is ambiguous, ask **one clarifying question** rather than assuming
- If two reasonable options exist, **recommend one and explain why**
- Do not refactor outside the current task's scope unless it causes a type error or test failure
- When adding a dependency, justify it in one sentence in the commit message

---

## Hosting & Deployment Rules

- Hostable via **Docker Compose** with a single `docker compose up`
- `packages/app` → **nginx** container serving built Vite static assets
- `packages/tracer` → **uvicorn** container running FastAPI
- The tracer container is **never exposed on the host** — nginx proxies `/api/*`
  to the tracer internally within the Docker bridge network
- Both containers must define a **health check** in `docker-compose.yml`
- All ports, CORS origins, and environment config live in a `.env` file; a
  `.env.example` with every key documented must be committed to the repo
- A `Makefile` at root exposes: `make dev`, `make build`, `make up`, `make down`, `make test`
- Production nginx config must include gzip compression and correct cache
  headers (`immutable` for hashed assets, `no-cache` for `index.html`)

---

## Security Rules (Local Execution)

- All user code runs inside language-specific sandboxes — no raw `exec()` or `eval()`
- Python: `RestrictedPython` — block file I/O, network, subprocess
- JavaScript: Node.js `vm` module with a restricted context — no `require`,
  no `process`, no `fs`
- Java: compile to temp dir, run with a `SecurityManager` policy blocking
  file and network access
- C#: Roslyn scripting with restricted imports — no `System.IO`, no `System.Net`
- All tracers: hard-kill execution after **5 seconds**
- FastAPI binds to `127.0.0.1` in dev; in Docker it binds to `0.0.0.0` only
  within the internal Docker network — never exposed directly on the host
